@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ito-il27-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-il27-tax-years`
IMPORT `ito-s41-spouse-married-part-year`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Tests for s 41. Row IL-27. Expected values worked by hand from lines 1690-1692 before the rules were run; none edited.
-- Points = (months not married x whole-year points under ss 34, 36, 40(b), 40B + months married x whole-year points under s 66) / 12.
-- The whole-year points are inputs: here 3 (unmarried) and 6 (married), chosen for easy arithmetic; they are not the answers of ss 34-40B or 66.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Tests — section 41`

-- The fields: tax year; registered spouse; months not married; months married; months married for part; points unmarried; points under s 66.
GIVEN `the year`    IS A NUMBER
      `not`         IS A NUMBER
      `married`     IS A NUMBER
      `part`        IS A NUMBER
      `unmarried points` IS A NUMBER
      `s 66 points` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A spouse married for part of the tax year, for section 41`
`in` `the year` `, months not married` `not` `, married` `married` `, part` `part` `; points unmarried` `unmarried points` `and under s 66` `s 66 points` MEANS
    `A spouse married for part of the tax year, for section 41` OF `the year`, FALSE, `not`, `married`, `part`, `unmarried points`, `s 66 points`

§§ `No month of part marriage`

-- 5 months not married and 7 married: (5 x 3 + 7 x 6) / 12 = (15 + 42) / 12 = 57/12 = 19/4.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 41 for` (`in` 2026 `, months not married` 5 `, married` 7 `, part` 0 `; points unmarried` 3 `and under s 66` 6) EQUALS 19/4
-- A whole year unmarried: 12 x 3 / 12 = 3. A whole year married: 12 x 6 / 12 = 6.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 41 for` (`in` 2026 `, months not married` 12 `, married` 0 `, part` 0 `; points unmarried` 3 `and under s 66` 6) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 41 for` (`in` 2026 `, months not married` 0 `, married` 12 `, part` 0 `; points unmarried` 3 `and under s 66` 6) EQUALS 6
-- Married in the last month only: 11 x 3 + 1 x 6 = 39; 39/12 = 13/4. Married in the first month only: 1 x 6 + 11 x 3 -> the same here by symmetry of the formula.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 41 for` (`in` 2026 `, months not married` 11 `, married` 1 `, part` 0 `; points unmarried` 3 `and under s 66` 6) EQUALS 13/4
-- The year of the row's range: 2024 answers; 2023 is refused by the general gate.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 41 for` (`in` 2024 `, months not married` 5 `, married` 7 `, part` 0 `; points unmarried` 3 `and under s 66` 6) EQUALS 19/4
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 41 for` (`in` 2023 `, months not married` 5 `, married` 7 `, part` 0 `; points unmarried` 3 `and under s 66` 6) BECAUSE "row IL-27 does not hold the text of these sections for a tax year before 2024"

§§ `Fork F6 — a month in which he was married for part`

-- 5 not married, 6 married, 1 married for part. As married: (5 x 3 + 7 x 6) / 12 = 57/12 = 19/4. As not married: (6 x 3 + 6 x 6) / 12 = 54/12 = 9/2.
-- As neither: (5 x 3 + 6 x 6) / 12 = 51/12 = 17/4. The default declines.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 41, reading a month married for part as` `a month in which he was married` `, for` (`in` 2026 `, months not married` 5 `, married` 6 `, part` 1 `; points unmarried` 3 `and under s 66` 6) EQUALS 19/4
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 41, reading a month married for part as` `a month in which he was not married` `, for` (`in` 2026 `, months not married` 5 `, married` 6 `, part` 1 `; points unmarried` 3 `and under s 66` 6) EQUALS 9/2
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 41, reading a month married for part as` `a month of neither` `, for` (`in` 2026 `, months not married` 5 `, married` 6 `, part` 1 `; points unmarried` 3 `and under s 66` 6) EQUALS 17/4
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 41 for` (`in` 2026 `, months not married` 5 `, married` 6 `, part` 1 `; points unmarried` 3 `and under s 66` 6) BECAUSE "section 41 does not say in which list a month of part marriage is, and here the readings differ"
-- With equal points of 4 on both sides: as married (5 + 7) x 4 / 12 = 4; as not married (6 + 6) x 4 / 12 = 4; as neither (5 + 6) x 4 / 12 = 11/3.
-- The third reading differs, so the default still declines.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 41 for` (`in` 2026 `, months not married` 5 `, married` 6 `, part` 1 `; points unmarried` 4 `and under s 66` 4) BECAUSE "section 41 does not say in which list a month of part marriage is, and here the readings differ"
-- With no points at all the readings agree: 0.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 41 for` (`in` 2026 `, months not married` 5 `, married` 6 `, part` 1 `; points unmarried` 0 `and under s 66` 0) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `section 41 — the reading row IL-27 takes of a month in which he was married for part` EQUALS `declined where the readings differ`

§§ `Registered spouse; months that do not add up`

#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 41 for` (`A spouse married for part of the tax year, for section 41` OF 2026, TRUE, 5, 7, 0, 3, 6) BECAUSE "section 41 does not apply to a registered spouse, whose tax is under sections 64B and 65"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 41 for` (`in` 2026 `, months not married` 5 `, married` 5 `, part` 0 `; points unmarried` 3 `and under s 66` 6) BECAUSE "the months of the tax year given for section 41 do not add up to twelve"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 41 for` (`in` 2026 `, months not married` 6 `, married` 7 `, part` 0 `; points unmarried` 3 `and under s 66` 6) BECAUSE "the months of the tax year given for section 41 do not add up to twelve"
